@tradition knit-and-natter
// Knit and natter (0.60.7): Zeke's circle in the junior common room: knitting, sketching, reading together, any hobby
// welcome. On at the same time as Tiles night (another deck), so you pick one.
k: 444
title: Knit and natter
when: weekly tuesday
at: 20:00-21:30
min: 25
jitter: 15
where: 4 pool common-room
hold: 1
who: torres-zeke always, common-room 55%, quiet-corner 35%, juniors 20%, everyone 6%
anim: read
host: torres-zeke
from: torres-zeke
invite: host=torres-zeke odds=35% line="Knit and natter tonight, common room. Bring whatever you're making. Or just come and natter."

== mail
- Knit and natter tomorrow, {time}, junior common room. Bring a hobby: needles, a sketchbook, a book. Or nothing. Tea's on me.

== ask
- Knit and natter tonight. Zeke's teaching me to purl. It's going badly.   #funny
- Bring your sketchbook to the common room later. Nobody looks unless you want them to.   #warm
- Knit and natter or Tiles tonight? Can't do both.

== here
- Hold it looser. The wool's not going anywhere.   #warm
- That's a scarf. It's definitely a scarf.   #funny
- Pass the blue, would you?

== thanks
- You sit down in Zeke's circle. Needles click, pencils scratch, and the talk is easy.   #warm

== chatter
- Zeke's knitted something for half the Works. Mostly socks.   #funny
- I finished a whole sketchbook at knit and natter.   #warm
